#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:103
msgid "VFIO Selftests Library (libvfio)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:105
msgid ""
"The selftests directory contains a helper library compiled from the ``lib/`` "
"subdirectory. It provides structures and helper functions to handle standard "
"operations like opening VFIO devices, creating VFIO containers, and "
"interacting with VFIO and IOMMUFD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:110
msgid ""
"All VFIO selftests have libvfio linked in by default. Tests can access the "
"library by including ``<libvfio.h>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:114
msgid "Core Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:116
msgid ""
"The VFIO selftests framework revolves around two distinct core objects: "
"``struct iommu`` and ``struct vfio_pci_device``. It is important to "
"understand the distinction and relationship between them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:120
msgid ""
"``struct iommu`` represents an IOMMU domain and the API used to program it "
"(e.g. legacy VFIO Type1 vs IOMMUFD). It is responsible for managing the I/O "
"address space, handling DMA mappings, and translating between host virtual "
"addresses (HVA) and IO virtual addresses (IOVA)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:125
msgid ""
"``struct vfio_pci_device`` represents a single PCI device. It encapsulates "
"the VFIO device file descriptor, handles access to the PCI configuration "
"space, manages memory-mapped BARs, and drives device interrupts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:129
msgid ""
"A typical test initializes an IOMMU instance first, then passes it when "
"initializing one or more PCI devices, linking the devices to the shared "
"IOMMU domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:134
msgid "``struct iommu``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:136
msgid ""
"The ``struct iommu`` abstracts away the complexity of managing VFIO "
"containers, IOMMU groups, and IOMMUFD contexts. A test allocates its IOMMU "
"handle using ``iommu_init()`` passing one of the supported IOMMU modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:146
msgid ""
"The selftest framework is designed to work uniformly across all standard "
"kernel IOMMU APIs. The defined modes (in ``iommu.h``) include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:149
msgid "``MODE_VFIO_TYPE1_IOMMU``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:150
msgid "``MODE_VFIO_TYPE1V2_IOMMU``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:151
msgid "``MODE_IOMMUFD_COMPAT_TYPE1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:152
msgid "``MODE_IOMMUFD_COMPAT_TYPE1V2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:153
msgid "``MODE_IOMMUFD``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:155
msgid ""
"VFIO selftests can replicate their test cases across all possible IOMMU "
"modes using FIXTURE_VARIANT_ADD_ALL_IOMMU_MODES() to ensure kernel IOMMU "
"APIs remain compatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:160
msgid "``struct vfio_pci_device``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:162
msgid ""
"A PCI device is represented as a ``struct vfio_pci_device``. The device "
"representation is initialized using ``vfio_pci_device_init()``, which takes "
"a target BDF string, opens the device in VFIO, and binds it to an existing "
"``struct iommu`` instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:174
msgid "``struct iova_allocator``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:176
msgid ""
"To facilitate DMA mappings without hardcoding IOVAs (IO virtual addresses) "
"that might conflict with reserved platform address ranges, the library "
"provides a ``struct iova_allocator``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:180
msgid ""
"The IOVA allocator queries the underlying IOMMU (via ``struct iommu``) for "
"its valid target IOVA ranges. Tests can safely carve out unique contiguous "
"chunks of IOVA space for device DMA by repeatedly calling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:190
msgid "Driver Framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:192
msgid ""
"The primary goal of VFIO selftests is to verify the correctness of the "
"kernel code handling VFIO devices, including VFIO core, IOMMUFD, IOMMU "
"drivers, page pinning, DMA mapping/unmapping, interrupt remapping, and IRQ "
"delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:196
msgid ""
"Because different physical devices have vastly different programming "
"interfaces for triggering work, the selftests library implements a standard "
"driver framework.  This framework abstracts diverse hardware endpoints (such "
"as Intel IGB, IOAT, or DSA) behind a uniform interface, allowing tests to "
"provoke a broad range of devices to generate DMA operations and interrupts "
"in a standardized manner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:203
msgid ""
"By exercising DMA and interrupts with real endpoints, tests can thoroughly "
"stress and validate the underlying kernel paths, such as IOMMU page table "
"management, dirty page tracking, Device TLB and IOTLB invalidations, and "
"interrupt delivery under authentic hardware conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:208
msgid ""
"All endpoint driver implementations populate a common set of operations "
"defined in ``struct vfio_pci_driver_ops``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:211
msgid ""
"``probe()``: Validate whether the driver supports the current PCI device "
"(e.g. matching vendor/device IDs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:213
msgid ""
"``init()``: Set up specific control registers or ring-buffer data structures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:214
msgid "``remove()``: Clean up structures before destruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:215
msgid "``memcpy_start()``: Initiate DMA copies via the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:216
msgid ""
"``memcpy_wait()``: Poll and wait until previously initiated copies complete "
"safely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:218
msgid "``send_msi()``: Provoke the device to signal an MSI interrupt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:220
msgid ""
"Tests are required to set up a dedicated DMA region for the driver to use "
"within ``struct vfio_pci_driver`` to serve as the driver's main memory "
"allocation region (e.g. used for in-memory descriptor rings and hardware "
"buffers). Tests must provision and map this DMA region before completing "
"driver initialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:226
msgid ""
"For a complete example of interacting with the driver framework from a test "
"perspective, refer to ``tools/testing/selftests/vfio/"
"vfio_pci_driver_test.c``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:229
msgid ""
"When contributing a new driver implementation to the selftests library, the "
"primary acceptance criteria is that ``vfio_pci_driver_test`` passes using "
"the new driver and target device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:234
msgid "Integration with KVM Selftests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:236
msgid ""
"libvfio is not strictly limited to VFIO selftests, it is also leveraged "
"within KVM selftests (``tools/testing/selftests/kvm/``). KVM selftests build "
"their own copy of libvfio and link against it, enabling libvfio to be used "
"in KVM selftests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:241
msgid ""
"This integration enables testing the interaction between KVM and VFIO and "
"IOMMUFD. For example, testing the end-to-end delivery of device interrupts "
"into running vCPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:246
msgid "Contribution Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:248
msgid ""
"Prefer the shortlog prefix ``vfio: selftests: ...`` for commits that modify "
"files in ``tools/testing/selftests/vfio/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/vfio-selftests.rst:250
msgid ""
"Follow the Coding Style, Comments, Changelogs, and Function References "
"guidelines from the :doc:`KVM x86 maintainers handbook </process/maintainer-"
"kvm-x86>`."
msgstr ""
